WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.300
The man stands in the same place he's been for the past 13 years

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:07.380
writing out his life story for everyone to witness.

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.060
And yet...

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:11.640
when they realize what it actually is...

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.400
they'll see me.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.960
Hello everybody, my name is Markplier and welcome

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.400
to Markiplier makes fan fiction

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:26.300
I am your 'host' of sorts. Although I may be donning this outfit, I will not be hosting you today.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.300
No, we

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.380
will be writing for you.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:31.960
Introducing-

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.400
Introducing Tyler.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:40.900
He's a man who stands alone writing in a lofty lighthouse on the side of the sea.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:48.700
Also introducing Ethan, who's been writing in his basement alone for years. His grandchildren never call.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.540
But when he makes this book, what's it called?

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.000
Ethan: Horses...

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.640
...Presidents?

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:56.900
Mark: Keep working on that.

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.120
*Laughing*

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:01.900
When he finishes this book, it'll take the world by storm.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.000
Twilight? *psh* Whatever.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Killing games? *chh*

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:06.780
No.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.080
Not at all.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:14.100
But we're not just here to write fan fiction for you. We're here to write fan fiction for us.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.740
So what we need from you is a suggestion for an idea.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.180
Wait, what was your grandma character?

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.360
Ethan: Mrs. Thompson.

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:23.320
Mark: Mrs. Thompson!

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.200
(Ethan: Hell yeah) Mark: Thank you so much for joining us, Mrs. Thompson.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.820
Do you know how to use that technology device?

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:34.000
Ethan: *Old lady voice* Oh, I don't think I know how to use a cellular device. 'Ere.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.920
Mark: No, you figure it out. *Mark and Tyler Laugh*

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:42.220
While we're waiting for your responses, let me give you a little taste of the history of writing.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.760
Back in the year 1922

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:50.500
the typewriter was invented by a man named Yorkshireman von Der Beek

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:58.200
And he looked at his piece of paper and pen and was like, "This is just ridiculous. Who could? Who would?

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:03.880
Who should?" And he cried out to the heavens and the devils and he said, "Please?"

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.900
"Lord, give me a sign! How do I lead us into the age of enlightenment?"

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:10.900
And BOOM!

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.900
The typewriter fell from the sky.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.800
*bang bang*

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:15.800
